# FIXED DEFECT 411's shape beside `tests/golden/fixedbugs/ffi-call-arity`,
# 2026-10-07, lane b13-w411.
#
# SYMPTOM, on the round that took the repair: a binding whose parameter count
# disagrees with the header's was told only that its first `cstr` may be
# written, and the count it got wrong was not told at all, since the pointee
# check that asks the read-only question runs before the probe that tells the
# count.
#
# CAUSE: the question names a header parameter by POSITION, and with the counts
# apart the position is unknown. Here the header takes `(char *x, const char
# *a, const char *b)` and the binding declares `(a, b)`: asked by position, `a`
# would be told it may be written, which is false of the header's `a`.
#
# FIX: `emit/ffi_read_only.hero`'s `lend_answers` asks a function's read-only
# questions only where its declared count is the header's, so this binding is
# told its count, `ffi_call_shape`, and nothing false.

extern "fixedbugs-411-writes.h"
    function w_shifted(a: cstr lent, b: cstr lent) -> i32  #~ ffi_call_shape

function main()
    print(w_shifted(a: "a".cstr(), b: "b".cstr()))
